But this nesting is too deep and repeats. Actually we need each intermediate node only once. Simpler: Use separate nodes without children for intermediates, just reaction nodes linking them.

Structure:

Root mol -> reaction 1040 children: intermediate3 mol, H2O2 mol.

Intermediate3 mol -> reaction 1030 children: intermediate2 mol, 3-buten-1-ol mol.

Intermediate2 mol -> reaction 1020 children: intermediate1 mol, H2 mol.

Intermediate1 mol -> reaction 1010 children: cyclohexanone mol, MVK mol.

Leaves: cyclohexanone, MVK, H2, 3-buten-1-ol, H2O2.

